# B2 — resource leak (CWE-772, VYQL-RES-001). A type-state rule: a handle allocated but
# not released on EVERY path to function exit leaks. `closed_by` is a POST-dominance check
# over the structured CFG — a close in only one branch does not cover the others.

test "resource-leak: a socket closed on every path is clean (python)"
  lang python
  reject VYQL-RES-001
  code
  ```
  import socket
  def f():
      s = socket.socket()
      s.close()
  ```

test "resource-leak: a socket never closed leaks (python)"
  lang python
  expect VYQL-RES-001
  code
  ```
  import socket
  def f():
      s = socket.socket()
      s.send(b"x")
  ```

test "resource-leak: a socket closed only in one branch leaks on the others (python)"
  lang python
  expect VYQL-RES-001
  code
  ```
  import socket
  def f(cond):
      s = socket.socket()
      if cond:
          s.close()
  ```
